# valgrind suppressions for the Qore tests
#
# run_tests.sh passes this file to every valgrind that a test starts (VALGRIND_OPTS); give it to a manual run with
# --suppressions=examples/test/valgrind.supp.  An entry suppresses a report in a library that Qore uses, which is not
# an error of Qore, and names the exact frames of the report, never a whole library: a report of Qore's own code is
# never suppressed (see examples/test/qore/misc/valgrind-suppressions.qtest, which checks that a read of a value that
# was never written and a use-after-free in Qore's code, and a value that was never written that Qore's code passes to
# an LLVM call, are still reported).
#
# LLVM 21 (libLLVM.so.21.1, Ubuntu's build, arm64), with valgrind 3.22.0 (also with --expensive-definedness-checks=yes):
# every optimized JIT compile reports "Conditional jump or move depends on uninitialised value(s)" in the two frames
# below.  Both are reproduced by a program that makes only the calls of Qore's JIT (optimizeModule() and the code
# emission of lib/QoreJIT.cpp) on a module of one function, with no Qore code:
#   - buildModuleSimplificationPipeline(): the uninitialised bytes are the payload of PassBuilder::PGOOpt, an empty
#     std::optional<PGOOptions> (found by marking each region of a zero-filled PassBuilder undefined with
#     VALGRIND_MAKE_MEM_UNDEFINED); the source tests that the optional has a value before it reads it, and the arm64
#     code reads the payload with the test in a conditional compare (ccmp), which memcheck does not track exactly (as
#     in https://bugs.kde.org/show_bug.cgi?id=485276)
#   - emitPatchableFunctionEntries(): the uninitialised value is a local variable of the function itself
# The JIT runs in tests that check other code under valgrind whenever a Program compiles code (ex: tiered execution),
# so that such a test failed with these reports (enum-decl-copy-outlives-original.qtest).
{
   llvm21-passbuilder-pgoopt-arm64-ccmp
   Memcheck:Cond
   fun:_ZN4llvm11PassBuilder33buildModuleSimplificationPipelineENS_17OptimizationLevelENS_18ThinOrFullLTOPhaseE
   fun:_ZN4llvm11PassBuilder29buildPerModuleDefaultPipelineENS_17OptimizationLevelENS_18ThinOrFullLTOPhaseE
}
{
   llvm21-asmprinter-patchable-function-entries
   Memcheck:Cond
   fun:_ZN4llvm10AsmPrinter28emitPatchableFunctionEntriesEv
   fun:_ZN4llvm10AsmPrinter16emitFunctionBodyEv
}
#
# LLVM 21.1 on aarch64 only (/usr/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu/libLLVM.so.21.1, Ubuntu's build), with valgrind 3.22.0:
# InstCombine reports "Conditional jump or move depends on uninitialised value(s)" for a binary operator (add, sub, mul,
# and, or, xor) whose first operand is a select and whose second is not.  The five innermost frames are functions of
# libLLVM that its dynamic symbol table does not name (identified in the disassembly):
# InstCombinerImpl::SimplifySelectsFeedingBinaryOp() <- foldUsingDistributiveLaws() <- the visitor of the operator
# (visitAnd() for Qore's code) <- InstCombinerImpl::run() <- combineInstructionsOverFunction(), under
# InstCombinePass::run().  The source tests "LHSIsSelect && RHSIsSelect && A == D", and the aarch64 code evaluates
# A == D without a branch (cmp, csel, and), reading D, a local variable that only a select as the second operand
# writes (valgrind --track-origins=yes: "created by a stack allocation" in that function); the csel gives 0 either
# way, but memcheck makes its result undefined when its condition is.  The JIT on amd64 has no such report.  Qore's
# JIT emits this shape when emitWeakSharedTest() (lib/QoreIRToLLVM.cpp) masks the pointer of a value that
# emitHelperRef() selected (the weak share check of a store, qore#7342), ex: "int s; for (...) { s += i * 2; }"
# (examples/test/ir/jit-teardown-at-exit/JitTeardownAtExit.qr; valgrind-suppressions.qtest compiles such code).
# examples/test/valgrind-repro/llvm21-instcombine-csel/ reproduces it with no Qore code and the same libLLVM frames:
# run.sh runs LLVM's own opt on f.ll (a select feeding an "and") and instcombine_select_and.cpp, a program that makes
# only the calls of optimizeModule() (lib/QoreJIT.cpp) on the same function.  Remove the entry when LLVM is fixed
# (qore#7729).
# The entries match only InstCombine run by the JIT's optimizeModule() for compileFunctionInternal() and for
# compileFunctionBatchInternal() (a function compiled with the functions that it calls, ex: f() calling such a g()),
# the same stack in a background and a synchronous compile (QORE_JIT_SYNC_COMPILE=1; both run on the JIT's compile
# thread): the five frames of libLLVM by their object, as they have no names, and the named frames down to Qore's code,
# eleven frames, within valgrind's default --num-callers of 12 (the frames of the static optimizeModule() are those of
# a debug build, which the CI test jobs test).  LLVM's own opt reports the same frame of InstCombine, with the same
# origin, on the code of a Qore module compiled by qcc (the batch entry: qore#7765, seen on aarch64 only).
{
   llvm21-instcombine-select-binop-arm64-csel
   Memcheck:Cond
   obj:*/aarch64-linux-gnu/libLLVM.so.21.1
   obj:*/aarch64-linux-gnu/libLLVM.so.21.1
   obj:*/aarch64-linux-gnu/libLLVM.so.21.1
   obj:*/aarch64-linux-gnu/libLLVM.so.21.1
   obj:*/aarch64-linux-gnu/libLLVM.so.21.1
   fun:_ZN4llvm15InstCombinePass3runERNS_8FunctionERNS_15AnalysisManagerIS1_JEEE
   fun:_ZN4llvm11PassManagerINS_8FunctionENS_15AnalysisManagerIS1_JEEEJEE3runERS1_RS3_
   fun:_ZN4llvm27ModuleToFunctionPassAdaptor3runERNS_6ModuleERNS_15AnalysisManagerIS1_JEEE
   fun:_ZN4llvm11PassManagerINS_6ModuleENS_15AnalysisManagerIS1_JEEEJEE3runERS1_RS3_
   fun:_ZL14optimizeModuleRN4llvm6ModuleEiPKSt6atomicIbE
   fun:_ZN7QoreJIT23compileFunctionInternalERK14QoreIRFunctionRNSt7__cxx1112basic_stringIcSt11char_traitsIcESaIcEEEPvPKS8_
}
{
   llvm21-instcombine-select-binop-arm64-csel-batch
   Memcheck:Cond
   obj:*/aarch64-linux-gnu/libLLVM.so.21.1
   obj:*/aarch64-linux-gnu/libLLVM.so.21.1
   obj:*/aarch64-linux-gnu/libLLVM.so.21.1
   obj:*/aarch64-linux-gnu/libLLVM.so.21.1
   obj:*/aarch64-linux-gnu/libLLVM.so.21.1
   fun:_ZN4llvm15InstCombinePass3runERNS_8FunctionERNS_15AnalysisManagerIS1_JEEE
   fun:_ZN4llvm11PassManagerINS_8FunctionENS_15AnalysisManagerIS1_JEEEJEE3runERS1_RS3_
   fun:_ZN4llvm27ModuleToFunctionPassAdaptor3runERNS_6ModuleERNS_15AnalysisManagerIS1_JEEE
   fun:_ZN4llvm11PassManagerINS_6ModuleENS_15AnalysisManagerIS1_JEEEJEE3runERS1_RS3_
   fun:_ZL14optimizeModuleRN4llvm6ModuleEiPKSt6atomicIbE
   fun:_ZN7QoreJIT28compileFunctionBatchInternalERK14QoreIRFunctionRNSt7__cxx1112basic_stringIcSt11char_traitsIcESaIcEEEPvRKSt6vectorINS_11BatchCalleeESaISC_EEPS0_
}
